# DD1: the dispatch diagnostic for the ~16 us stalls before conv-gates users 1-3 (QWEN_FAST_GDN_DISPATCH_DIAG). c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-dispatchdiag is the control plus EXACTLY the flag, which records host time only and
# changes no op. It runs on the control recipe because that is where each layer launches four per-user conv-gates programs (V1 makes it one). Read the container log: the first eight
# '[PINDIAG] tp4 gdn dispatch diag call=k ops=N conv_gates=4 ops_between_conv_gates=[a, b, c] host_gap_us=[...] host_span_us=S' lines (one per packed GDN decode call: the eager warm forward and the capture).
# What they decide: if ops_between_conv_gates is [0, 0, 0] the four launches are enqueued back to back, so a 15 us spacing of independent ops between them (the exact fallback in the diagnosis) is
# available only by moving the z slices and the other per-user ops, which are enqueued after each launch; if the enqueue gaps are far above 16 us the host is not what the device waits on. The
# DEVICE side (whether the dispatcher waits for the previous conv-gates to retire before staging the next program's config) needs TT_METAL_DEVICE_PROFILER_DISPATCH=1 on a profiled arm, which a profile
# env may not carry (ops_profile_plan refuses TT_METAL_* in a profile): a profile job adding it to ops-trace is the follow-up. Smoke only here.
# Duration (estimate): 30-45 min. OPTIONAL: data only.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/gluefix window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/gluefix and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-gluefix-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for ONE FRESH tag (never used before) that B0 builds from the pushed tp4/gluefix commit while production
# serves; the driver substitutes it in every template. A reused tag is skipped by the build step and would silently serve an old image.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-gluefix-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-dispatchdiag
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent4_code_equal
